From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phone-rpc: map exact camera metadata input read-only

Run77 requested one camera metadata input outside the existing sensors tree.
Expose only that fixed virtual filename from an optional staged camera file.
Missing data stays ENOENT. Neither the camera directory nor host persist tree is
passed through, and the file is outside the volatile writable namespace.

The private input is deliberately absent from this source patch and artifacts.
Tests use synthetic binary bytes including NUL, verify missing/read/EOF/seek,
neighbor and traversal refusal, and exercise read/write rejection through the
real apps_std wire dispatcher. No camera or sensor client is started.

--- a/hexagonrpcd/rpcd_builder.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/rpcd_builder.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #define ODM_SENSORS_CONFIG	"/sensors/odm-config/"
 #define SYSFS_SOCINFO		"/socinfo/"
 #define PHONE_PCB_VERSION	"/board/pcbVersion"
+#define PHONE_CAMERA_INFO	"/camera/Rear_third_camera_info.bin"
 
 static struct hexagonfs_dirent *hfs_mkdir(const char *name, size_t n_ents, ...)
 {
@@ -117,7 +118,7 @@
